IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra1-three-valued`
IMPORT `wra1-ch2-responsibilities`

-- Tests for wra1-ch2-responsibilities.l4 (sections 13 to 29). Every expected value is written by hand from the text quoted in
-- the module, beside the assertion. A number such as 28 is an invented test figure unless the Act states it (13 weeks, 3 years,
-- 26 weeks). The regulative rules are run with #TRACE; the stable binary prints a #TRACE outcome and cannot assert it, so each
-- duty also has a decision-function twin, asserted below.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVETH A Period
`s 24(5) test: a period starting on 1 March 2026` MEANS `s 24(5) the period of 13 weeks` (Date 1 3 2026)

§ `s 13`

#ASSERT `s 13(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the section that defines the work-related requirement` `work-focused interview requirement` EQUALS "section 15"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the section that defines the work-related requirement` `work preparation requirement` EQUALS "section 16"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the section that defines the work-related requirement` `work search requirement` EQUALS "section 17"
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the section that defines the work-related requirement` `work availability requirement` EQUALS "section 18"
#ASSERT `s 13(3) the section that describes the group` `no work-related requirements` EQUALS "section 19"
#ASSERT `s 13(3) the section that describes the group` `work-focused interview requirement only` EQUALS "section 20"
#ASSERT `s 13(3) the section that describes the group` `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only` EQUALS "section 21"
#ASSERT `s 13(3) the section that describes the group` `all work-related requirements` EQUALS "section 22"

-- (1) the claimant's duty: complying fulfils it. The Act fixes no time (the time comes from the requirement imposed), so the rule
-- has no WITHIN and waiting never breaches it: the duty stays open (the outcome is the rule itself, printed back).
#TRACE `s 13(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement imposed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 13(1) the claimant` DOES `s 13(1) complies with the work-related requirement imposed` AT 10

#TRACE `s 13(1) the claimant must comply with the work-related requirement imposed` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§ `s 14`

#ASSERT `s 14(1) the document is a claimant commitment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(1) the document is a claimant commitment` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(2) this authority prepares, reviews and updates the claimant commitment` `the Secretary of State` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2) this authority prepares, reviews and updates the claimant commitment` `an authorised person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(2) this authority prepares, reviews and updates the claimant commitment` `a local authority` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(2) this authority prepares, reviews and updates the claimant commitment` `the First-tier Tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the claimant commitment is in the form the Secretary of State thinks fit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(3) the claimant commitment is in the form the Secretary of State thinks fit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the claimant commitment is to include` `s 14(4)(a) a record of the requirements the claimant must comply with` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the claimant commitment is to include` `s 14(4)(b) any prescribed information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the claimant commitment is to include` `s 14(4)(c) any other information the Secretary of State considers appropriate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(4) the claimant commitment is to include` `s 14(4) some other item` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) "if, and only if": both limbs are needed, and a missing limb is the text's no
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14(5) the claimant accepts the claimant commitment` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

